    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nI use the cursor trail feature in Kitty. When I open a scrollback buffer I get the following flash of moving cursor as Neovim sets the cursor to cell (1,1) before it gets restored by the kitty-scrollback.nvim plugin:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d95ed085-37d7-45fc-ae94-61d6c98d4c46\n\nIt’s annoying and it seems that I can’t turn the cursor off. \n\nI’ve tried the following to resolve the issue:\n\n1. Disabling the cursor with `printf '\\033[?25l'`. Doesn’t work. Seems like Neovim turns the cursor back on when it boots up.\n2. Blending the cursor with `--cmd \"hi Cursor blend=100\" --cmd \"set guicursor+=a:Cursor/lCursor\"`. Doesn’t work well. The cursor gets hidden only after the cursor travels back to the (1,1) cell.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThere are a few options this can be resolved:\n\n- Have Neovim honor terminal settings set by `\\033[?25` + possibly give an API for controlling it.\n- Provide a way command-line flag + runtime API for disabling the cursor. One should have the control for when cursor should show up or not over the whole lifetime of the process, not just after `init.lua` has been loaded.\n\nI would appreciate any insight here to resolve my original problem.",
